# cosign public key

`deploy/v3/cosign.pub` is generated by the operator on the offline signing
machine and committed here. It is the only key `tools/release.sh verify` trusts
by default.

```bash
cosign generate-key-pair
# keep cosign.key offline; commit the generated cosign.pub as deploy/v3/cosign.pub
```

The private key is never committed, never in CI, never a workflow secret, and
never in an agent environment. This example file is not a key and must not be
copied to `cosign.pub`; verification fails closed until the real public key
exists.

Rotation: sign the new release with the new key, replace `deploy/v3/cosign.pub`,
and keep prior keys under `deploy/v3/keys/<YYYY-MM-DD>/cosign.pub` for old
digests. Do not delete a public key that a supported release still cites.
